1432 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Address Book System is a C++-based application developed to store and manage contact information in an organized manner. The system stores details such as contact ID, name, phone number, email, address, and city. It provides various operations including adding, displaying, searching, updating, deleting, sorting, and counting contacts. The system also validates phone numbers, prevents duplicate phone numbers, and automatically assigns a unique ID to each contact. The project demonstrates important Object-Oriented Programming concepts such as classes, objects, encapsulation, constructors, and member functions. The application is implemented entirely in C++ and runs through the Command Prompt \(CMD\) using a simple menu-driven interface.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1365 0 R
>>
endobj
